{"words": [{"text": "أُحِلَّ", "translation": "Permitted"}, {"text": "لَكُمْ", "translation": "for you"}, {"text": "لَيْلَةَ", "translation": "(in the) nights"}, {"text": "ٱلصِّيَامِ", "translation": "(of) fasting"}, {"text": "ٱلرَّفَثُ", "translation": "(is) the approach"}, {"text": "إِلَىٰ", "translation": "to"}, {"text": "نِسَآئِكُمْ ۚ", "translation": "your wives"}, {"text": "هُنَّ", "translation": "They"}, {"text": "لِبَاسٌۭ", "translation": "(are) garments"}, {"text": "لَّكُمْ", "translation": "for you"}, {"text": "وَأَنتُمْ", "translation": "and you"}, {"text": "لِبَاسٌۭ", "translation": "(are) garments"}, {"text": "لَّهُنَّ ۗ", "translation": "for them"}, {"text": "عَلِمَ", "translation": "Knows"}, {"text": "ٱللَّهُ", "translation": "Allah"}, {"text": "أَنَّكُمْ", "translation": "that you"}, {"text": "كُنتُمْ", "translation": "used to"}, {"text": "تَخْتَانُونَ", "translation": "deceive"}, {"text": "أَنفُسَكُمْ", "translation": "yourselves"}, {"text": "فَتَابَ", "translation": "so He turned"}, {"text": "عَلَيْكُمْ", "translation": "towards you"}, {"text": "وَعَفَا", "translation": "and He forgave"}, {"text": "عَنكُمْ ۖ", "translation": "[on] you"}, {"text": "فَٱلْـَٔـٰنَ", "translation": "So now"}, {"text": "بَـٰشِرُوهُنَّ", "translation": "have relations with them"}, {"text": "وَٱبْتَغُوا۟", "translation": "and seek"}, {"text": "مَا", "translation": "what"}, {"text": "كَتَبَ", "translation": "has ordained"}, {"text": "ٱللَّهُ", "translation": "Allah"}, {"text": "لَكُمْ ۚ", "translation": "for you"}, {"text": "وَكُلُوا۟", "translation": "And eat"}, {"text": "وَٱشْرَبُوا۟", "translation": "and drink"}, {"text": "حَتَّىٰ", "translation": "until"}, {"text": "يَتَبَيَّنَ", "translation": "becomes distinct"}, {"text": "لَكُمُ", "translation": "to you"}, {"text": "ٱلْخَيْطُ", "translation": "the thread"}, {"text": "ٱلْأَبْيَضُ", "translation": "[the] white"}, {"text": "مِنَ", "translation": "from"}, {"text": "ٱلْخَيْطِ", "translation": "the thread"}, {"text": "ٱلْأَسْوَدِ", "translation": "[the] black"}, {"text": "مِنَ", "translation": "of"}, {"text": "ٱلْفَجْرِ ۖ", "translation": "[the] dawn"}, {"text": "ثُمَّ", "translation": "Then"}, {"text": "أَتِمُّوا۟", "translation": "complete"}, {"text": "ٱلصِّيَامَ", "translation": "the fast"}, {"text": "إِلَى", "translation": "till"}, {"text": "ٱلَّيْلِ ۚ", "translation": "the night"}, {"text": "وَلَا", "translation": "And (do) not"}, {"text": "تُبَـٰشِرُوهُنَّ", "translation": "have relations with them"}, {"text": "وَأَنتُمْ", "translation": "while you"}, {"text": "عَـٰكِفُونَ", "translation": "(are) secluded"}, {"text": "فِى", "translation": "in"}, {"text": "ٱلْمَسَـٰجِدِ ۗ", "translation": "the masajid"}, {"text": "تِلْكَ", "translation": "These"}, {"text": "حُدُودُ", "translation": "(are the) limits"}, {"text": "ٱللَّهِ", "translation": "(set by) Allah"}, {"text": "فَلَا", "translation": "so (do) not"}, {"text": "تَقْرَبُوهَا ۗ", "translation": "approach them"}, {"text": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translation": "Thus"}, {"text": "يُبَيِّنُ", "translation": "makes clear"}, {"text": "ٱللَّهُ", "translation": "Allah"}, {"text": "ءَايَـٰتِهِۦ", "translation": "His verses"}, {"text": "لِلنَّاسِ", "translation": "for [the] people"}, {"text": "لَعَلَّهُمْ", "translation": "so that they may"}, {"text": "يَتَّقُونَ", "translation": "(become) righteous"}], "sahih": "It has been made permissible for you the night preceding fasting to go to your wives [for sexual relations]. They are a clothing for you and you are a clothing1 for them. Allāh knows that you used to deceive yourselves,2 so He accepted your repentance and forgave you. So now, have relations with them and seek that which Allāh has decreed for you [i.e., offspring]. And eat and drink until the white thread of dawn becomes distinct to you from the black thread [of night]. Then complete the fast until the night [i.e., sunset]. And do not have relations with them as long as you are staying for worship in the mosques. These are the limits [set by] Allāh, so do not approach them. Thus does Allāh make clear His verses [i.e., ordinances] to the people that they may become righteous."}